      "message": "Well, we usually do it with a pure NDK header and then a platform header, and let the build system pick it.\n\nWe also have other ad hoc stuff:\nhttps://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:frameworks/native/libs/binder/ndk/include_cpp/android/binder_interface_utils.h;l\u003d46;drc\u003d163415a4de2fddee1d5b9760abe3f465ab2cc5a4\n\nThe NDK has an official build system, but it may be built in other ways, so I would suggest reversing the direction (define something only for platform builds). That will make it easier for app developers to adopt this.\n\nor split the headers out like libbinder_ndk",
